# PaykanLang clang-tidy configuration.
#
# Bug-focused, blocking gate: only the high-signal families that catch real
# defects are enabled, and findings are treated as errors in CI. Stylistic
# families (readability/modernize/misc namespace & include rules) are
# intentionally left off so the gate stays low-noise and actionable.
#
# clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling is off:
# in every C11 translation unit (the runtime, the test plugin modules) it
# flags each memcpy/memset/snprintf and asks for the Annex K *_s functions,
# which neither glibc nor macOS provides.  It only fired on Linux, where those
# calls reach the checker by name; macOS's fortified headers turn them into
# __builtin___*_chk calls it does not match, so CI never saw it.
#
# Off since LLVM 22, which added them, because what they flag is how this code
# is meant to be written, not a defect:
# - bugprone-derived-method-shadowing-base-method: a CRTP visitor's derived
#   class defines the visit methods the base class dispatches to
#   (ASTVisitor.h); that is the pattern, not shadowing by mistake.
# - bugprone-crtp-constructor-accessibility: the same visitors' public
#   default constructors.
# - bugprone-multi-level-implicit-pointer-conversion: `T **` to `void *`,
#   C's idiom for memcpy and the runtime's generic slots (Runtime.h).
# - performance-enum-size: an enum's underlying type is chosen for clarity,
#   not to save bytes in the few places one is stored.
# - clang-analyzer-security.ArrayBound (alpha.security.ArrayBoundV2 before,
#   never enabled here): it reports LLVM's own operand storage, which sits
#   before a User object, as out of bounds on any IRBuilder call; the report
#   is in LLVM's headers, so no NOLINT in our code reaches it.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  performance-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-narrowing-conversions,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  -bugprone-derived-method-shadowing-base-method,
  -bugprone-crtp-constructor-accessibility,
  -bugprone-multi-level-implicit-pointer-conversion,
  -performance-enum-size,
  -clang-analyzer-security.ArrayBound

WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*/(src|include)/.*\.h$'
FormatStyle: file
# A result discarded with `(void)` is discarded on purpose (a best-effort
# cleanup), as clang-tidy before LLVM 22 took it.
CheckOptions:
  bugprone-unused-return-value.AllowCastToVoid: true
